        {
          "title": "Beyond Search-Imitation: Prior-Directed Exploration for Searchless Chess",
          "title_zh": "超越搜索模仿：无搜索国际象棋中先验引导的探索",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27757v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.27757",
          "summary": "Fine-tunes a searchless chess network with self-play reinforcement learning, replacing the usual entropy bonus with a forward, mass-covering KL divergence toward the network's own MCTS prior, paired with an entropy-adaptive sampling temperature set by the value head's outcome uncertainty. In about two thousand steps it raises puzzle accuracy from 93.9% to 94.9% and mate-in-four accuracy from 77% to 81% while holding searchless strength at or slightly above the base, and a matched-compute sweep shows tactical accuracy and playing strength dissociate.",
