        {
          "title": "Informational Antilocality and the Locality Bias in LLMs",
          "title_zh": "信息反局部性与大语言模型中的局部性偏置",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27760v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.27760",
          "summary": "Constructs k-antilocal languages, which carry no mutual information across any span of k contiguous symbols, and trains transformer language models on them for increasing k. The models reach comparable cross-entropy loss regardless of antilocality but converge more slowly on more antilocal languages, supporting the view that non-local dependencies are harder to learn while locating the evidence in learning speed rather than learning success.",
