        {
          "title": "Memorization Is Not Extraction: Tight Differential-Privacy Bounds and Audit Blind Spots",
          "title_zh": "记忆不等于提取：紧致的差分隐私界与审计盲区",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27782v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.27782",
          "summary": "Pins down exact differential-privacy constants for counterfactual memorization and adaptive extraction under f-DP, showing that the two measures do not control each other and that DP uniformly controls extraction only up to a threshold in how well the secret can be guessed a priori, with min-entropy certifying that baseline distribution-free. It further derives a closed-form staircase bound for duplicated copies and constructs mechanisms that are either memorized yet unextractable or fully extractable yet invisible to loss-based scores, exposing a two-sided blind spot for loss-based auditing and unlearning verification.",
          "keywords": [
