        {
          "title": "Compositional Failure in Audio-Visual LLMs: Late-Layer Prior Dominance Under Cross-modal Conflict",
          "title_zh": "音视频大模型的组合性失败：跨模态冲突下的后层先验主导",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27785v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.27785",
          "summary": "Uses audio-visual conflict as a compositional generalization test, finding that VideoLLaMA 2-7B-AV stays near chance on the scored exact-string Yes/No subset of AVHBench across three alignment configurations, while off-the-shelf InternVideo2 shows a 32.3% accuracy decrease and a 17.3% instruction-following failure specifically under cross-modal conflict. A mechanistic analysis attributes this prior dominance to late-layer commitment around 25.5 ± 1 layers, and stronger temporal alignment changes answer bias without improving conflict resolution.",
