          "title": "What Can Low Resource Languages Learn From Each Other?",
          "title_zh": "低资源语言之间能相互学到什么？",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27753v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.27753",
          "summary": "Investigates OCR adaptation in extreme data-scarce regimes (under 10K real and under 250K synthetic images), observing that conventional fine-tuning reaches a ceiling and that specialized models diverge mainly in higher layers while lower layers learn redundant, highly similar features. The proposed PSMC framework derives language-specific experts from a high-resource base model and fuses them with task arithmetic, reporting roughly a 2% average Word Recognition Rate improvement across 10 Indian scripts (20+ languages) over individual specialists without increasing parameter count.",
